{"term":"bribe","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:31ac9e1c8b07974b1b","definition":"Something (usually money) given in exchange for influence or as an inducement to breaking the law.","example":"c. 1613-1625, Henry Hobart, Yardly v. Ellill\nUndue reward for anything against justice is a bribe.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["backhander","bribe","bung","payoff","coffee money","cold drink money","dash","douceur","inducement","kopi money","pay-off","payola","subornation","sweetener","tea money"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["bribeless","bribeproof","bribetaker","bribetaking"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bribe#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b7f34ec004c501c527","definition":"The act of offering or paying such a payment: an act of bribery.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["backhander","bribe","bung","payoff","coffee money","cold drink money","dash","douceur","inducement","kopi money","pay-off","payola","subornation","sweetener","tea money"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["bribeless","bribeproof","bribetaker","bribetaking"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bribe#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:eca8cfa9718757700c","definition":"That which seduces; seduction; allurement.","example":"Not the bribes of sordid wealth can seduce to leave these everblooming sweets.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["backhander","bribe","bung","payoff","coffee money","cold drink money","dash","douceur","inducement","kopi money","pay-off","payola","subornation","sweetener","tea money"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["bribeless","bribeproof","bribetaker","bribetaking"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contri